text.section:
To the extent specified by the board of directors or in the articles of incorporation or bylaws, each committee may exercise the authority of the board of directors under § 13.1-853, except that a committee may not:

Approve or recommend to members action that this Act requires to be approved by members;


Fill vacancies on the board or on any of its committees;


Amend the articles of incorporation pursuant to § 13.1-885;


Adopt, amend, or repeal the bylaws; or


Approve a plan of merger not requiring member approval.
